  "operative_text": "Section 29820 (Penal Code): (b) (1) Except as otherwise provided in paragraph (2), a person described in subdivision (a) shall not own, or have in possession or under custody or control, a firearm until the person is 30 years of age or older. (2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), a person who, on or after January 1, 2014, is adjudged a ward of the juvenile court within the meaning of Section 602 of the Welfare and Institutions Code because the person committed murder, attempted murder, or voluntary manslaughter shall not own, possess, or have custody or control of a firearm.\nSection 786 (Welfare and Institutions Code): (2) If a record described in paragraph (1) contains a sustained petition rendering the person ineligible to own or possess a firearm pursuant to paragraph (2) of subdivision (b) of Section 29820, then the sealed records shall not be destroyed."
}